Education savings accounts-income 25LSO-0582, 1.0
qualifications.
FISCAL NOTE
This bill creates an indeterminable expenditure increase from the Education Savings
Accounts Expenditure Account.
Under current law, subject to the availability of funds within the Education Savings
Accounts Expenditure Account, a child who is a Wyoming resident and whose household
income is at or below 150 percent of the federal poverty level, is eligible to
receive an education savings account equal to $6,000 per year. This bill increases
the number of education savings accounts that may be awarded from the Education
Savings Accounts Expenditure Account by adding two additional eligibility levels
based on federal poverty guidelines:
(i) An education savings account equal to $4,800 per year for a student's
household income more than 150 percent but equal to or less than 200
percent of the federal poverty level; and
(ii) An education savings account equal to $3,600 per year for a student's
household income more than 200 percent but equal to or less than 250
percent of the federal poverty level.
The 2024 federal poverty guidelines for the 48 contiguous states and the District
of Columbia, published by the United States Department of Health and Human Services,
are detailed below with columns indicating the 150 percent, 200 percent, and 250
percent eligibility requirement in this bill. The poverty guidelines for fiscal
year 2026 would be determined using the most recent federal poverty guidelines.
